eg} i \, < \, n\gamma\). ⟦36⟧ We have \(\mathop{
eg} i + 1 \leq n\gamma\). We have \(i \, < \, n\gamma + n\delta\) — immediate from its type. Define \(k = i - n\gamma\). We claim \(\mathbf{t}(i) =  rac{1 + c\delta(i - n\gamma)}{2}\): ⟦37⟧ We distinguish cases on \(i \leq n\gamma\). Case 1: \(i \leq n\gamma\). We have \(i = n\gamma\) — by integer arithmetic. We have \(n\gamma = n\gamma\) — by extensionality. Hence the claim, which is immediate from (7), (11), and (36). Case 2: \(\mathop{
eg} i \leq n\gamma\). ⟦38⟧ Hence the claim, which is immediate from (36) and (38). We claim \([\mathbf{t}(i), \mathbf{t}(i + 1)] \subseteq ((t : \mathbb{R}) \mapsto 2 \cdot t - 1)^{-1}([c\delta(k), c\delta(k + 1)])\): ⟦39⟧ Let \(t \in \mathbb{R}\) be given. Suppose \(t \in [\mathbf{t}(i), \mathbf{t}(i + 1)]\). ⟦40⟧ We have \(i + 1 - n\gamma = i - n\gamma + 1\) — by integer arithmetic. ⟦41⟧ First, \(c\delta(i - n\gamma) \leq 2 \cdot t - 1\), since \( i + 1 - n\gamma = i - n\gamma + 1 \). Second, \(2 \cdot t - 1 \leq c\delta(i - n\gamma + 1)\), since \( i + 1 - n\gamma = i - n\gamma + 1 \). We have \(((t : \mathbb{R}) \mapsto 2 \cdot t - 1) \in C^{\infty}\). ⟦42⟧ We have \(\delta \circ ((t : \mathbb{R}) \mapsto 2 \cdot t - 1) \in C^{\infty}([\mathbf{t}(i), \mathbf{t}(i + 1)])\) — by (13), (39), and (42). To show \(\operatorname{concat}(\gamma, \delta, t) = \delta(2 \cdot t - 1)\), we distinguish cases on \(t \leq  rac{1}{2}\). Case 1: \(t \leq  rac{1}{2}\). ⟦43⟧ We have \(\mathbf{t}(i) \leq t\). ⟦44⟧ We have \(c\delta(i - n\gamma) \geq 0\). ⟦45⟧ We have \(c\delta(i - n\gamma) = 0\), by (36) and by (37). ⟦46⟧ Define \(z = 0\). We have \(i - n\gamma = 0\) — by (11), (36), and (46). ⟦47⟧ Applying the same function to both sides of (47) gives \(i - n\gamma = 0\). ⟦48⟧ We have \(k = z\) — by extensionality, using (48). We have \(t =  rac{1}{2}\) — by (43), (44), and (45). It suffices to show \(  rac{1 + c\delta(i - n\gamma)}{2} \leq t \), by (37). Case 2: \(\mathop{
eg} t \leq  rac{1}{2}\). ⟦49⟧ Hence the claim, which is immediate from (49). Hence the claim.
